<div class="hero">
  <div class="hero-logo">💩🛍️</div>
  <h1>poop_bags</h1>
  <p class="tagline">
    Point it at a project directory. It bags the CRAP — <strong>C</strong>hange <strong>R</strong>isk <strong>A</strong>nti-<strong>P</strong>atterns —
    function by function, in Elixir, Zig, Kotlin, and Swift.
  </p>
</div>

<div class="card form-card">
  <.form for={%{}} action={~p"/scans"} method="post" class="scan-form">
    <div class="field">
      <label for="scan_project_path">Project directory</label>
      <input
        type="text"
        id="scan_project_path"
        name="scan[project_path]"
        placeholder="/absolute/path/to/project"
        required
        autofocus
      />
      <p class="hint">
        An absolute path on this machine. Build caches, .git, and vendored trees are skipped.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="field-row">
      <div class="field">
        <label for="scan_label">Label <span class="optional">(optional)</span></label>
        <input type="text" id="scan_label" name="scan[label]" placeholder="before the refactor" />
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="scan_threshold">
          Violation threshold <span class="optional">(optional)</span>
        </label>
        <input
          type="number"
          id="scan_threshold"
          name="scan[threshold]"
          value=""
          min="0"
          step="1"
          placeholder="20"
        />
        <p class="hint">
          CRAP above this counts as a violation for diffs and the CI gate. Blank = .poopbags.json or 20.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="scan_coverage">Assumed coverage %</label>
        <input
          type="number"
          id="scan_coverage"
          name="scan[coverage]"
          value="0"
          min="0"
          max="100"
          step="1"
        />
        <p class="hint">
          CRAP = comp² × (1 − cov)³ + comp. Leave blank to assume 0%. Real
          coverage comes from a report named in the project's
          <span class="mono">.poopbags.json</span>
          (LCOV or ExCoveralls JSON).
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <button type="submit" class="btn primary">Bag it</button>
  </.form>
</div>

<div class="card agent-card">
  <h2>For agents 🤖</h2>
  <p>
    Built agent-first: everything below is a stable JSON contract. The whole loop from a shell —
    start, poll, findings, diff:
  </p>
  <pre class="mono agent-recipe">
# 0. the service you're reading this from (dev runs :4100, production :4769)
HOST=http://localhost:4100

# 1. bag a project (absolute path on this machine; 202 + scan id)
curl -s $HOST/api/scans -H 'content-type: application/json' \
     -d '&#123;"project_path": "/abs/path/to/project", "coverage": 0&#125;'

# 2. poll until status is "done" (or "error")
curl -s $HOST/api/scans/$ID

# 3. worst-first findings (filter: ?language=zig&amp;limit=20)
curl -s "$HOST/api/scans/$ID/findings?limit=20"

# 4. outcomes vs the previous scan + gate verdict
curl -s "$HOST/api/scans/$ID/diff?against=latest"</pre>
  <ul class="agent-notes">
    <li>
      <span class="mono">GET /api</span> — the machine-readable contract (endpoints, semantics,
      gate rules, retention behavior) for discovering all of this without a browser.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>MCP server:</strong> <span class="mono">bin/poop_bags_mcp</span>
      in the repo exposes <span class="mono">bag_project</span>, <span class="mono">scan_status</span>, <span class="mono">top_findings</span>,
      <span class="mono">diff_latest</span>
      over stdio —
      wire it with <span class="mono">POOP_BAGS_URL</span>
      (default <span class="mono">http://localhost:4100</span>).
    </li>
    <li>
      From inside a checkout of this repo:
      <span class="mono">mix poop_bags.ci --path . --against latest</span>
      scans, diffs, gates,
      and exits 1 on new violations (2 on scan failure).
    </li>
    <li>
      The gate fails only on <em>introduced violations</em> or above-threshold regressions —
      refactors that resolve or improve never fail it.
    </li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h2>Recent scans</h2>

  <%= if @scans == [] do %>
    <p class="empty">Nothing bagged yet. The belts are warm.</p>
  <% else %>
    <table class="table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>#</th>
          <th>Project</th>
          <th>Status</th>
          <th>Files</th>
          <th>Functions</th>
          <th>Worst CRAP</th>
          <th>Avg CRAP</th>
          <th></th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <%= for scan <- @scans do %>
          <tr>
            <td class="mono">{scan.id}</td>
            <td>
              <.link href={~p"/scans/#{scan.id}"} class="project-link">
                <span class="project-name">{scan.label || Path.basename(scan.project_path)}</span>
                <span class="project-path mono">{scan.project_path}</span>
              </.link>
            </td>
            <td><span class={"status status-#{scan.status}"}>{scan.status}</span></td>
            <td class="mono">{scan.files_done}/{scan.files_total}</td>
            <td class="mono">{scan.functions_total}</td>
            <td class="mono">{scan.worst_crap}</td>
            <td class="mono">{scan.avg_crap}</td>
            <td>
              <.link href={~p"/scans/#{scan.id}"} class="btn small">open</.link>
            </td>
          </tr>
        <% end %>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  <% end %>
</div>
